WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.010
- [Narrator] This is iPhone City

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:05.400
a Foxconn manufacturing
campus in Zhengzhou ,China.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.460
With a population of as much as 300,000,

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.260
the size of Pittsburgh.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.110
The facility at one point made 85%

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.940
of the pro lineup of iPhones,

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.010
but now that's starting to change.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.590
Other Foxconn factories like
this one in southern India

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:21.480
have been tapped to build iPhones.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.030
And facilities like this
one in Vietnam are expanding

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.380
to produce other products

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.393
that were once mainly made in China.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.990
That's because protests
at the Zhengzhou factory

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:33.780
a wave of infections and
three years of Covid woes

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.770
in China, have helped propel
Apple to look for alternatives.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.140
But supply chain analysts
say China's finely tuned

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.410
production system won't
be easy to replace.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.590
So here's why Apple and its
suppliers face an uphill battle

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.260
when it comes to building
new iPhone Cities in India

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.193
and Vietnam.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.580
Over the past two decades

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.530
Apple has looked primarily to Foxconn,

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.410
the world's biggest electronics
manufacturing company,

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.080
to turn its product designs into reality.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.930
Since it first began
making iPhones in 2010

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.420
Foxconn's facility in
Zhengzhou has stood out

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.133
for its efficient ecosystem.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.820
It excels at collecting the
hundreds of required parts

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.030
from manufacturers, and
assembling the functioning devices

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.130
to be shipped out to customers.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.950
Supply chain analysts say,
China has been the best at this

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.140
because many of these
parts and the metals needed

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:25.530
to make them, are refined
and built within the country.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.600
But assembly plants in India and Vietnam

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.630
won't have such easy
access to these components.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:32.640
According to its latest list of suppliers

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.280
Apple works with more than 180 companies

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.550
and about 150 have operations in China.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.020
Just compare that to Vietnam

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.990
where only 26 Apple
suppliers have operations

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.240
while India only has 11.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.160
That means assemblers in these countries

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.290
would have to import
more of the parts needed

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:50.730
to make Apple products,

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:54.330
a process with plenty
of paperwork and delays.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.090
Once the parts arrive,
factories need a lot of workers

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:00.213
to assemble the many components
that go into Apple products.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.750
To maintain having hundreds
of thousands of workers

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.790
in iPhone City in Zhengzhou,

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:08.430
Foxconn provides onsite accommodation

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.710
that has allowed workers
from all around the country

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.080
to live and work at the factory.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.330
But India's Foxconn factory where Apple

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:17.520
is now building new
iPhones from the beginning

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.050
of their production cycle

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.360
is much smaller with fewer workers.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.850
So the company busses them
in from nearby hostels

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:27.600
and villages that are mostly
within a 50 mile radius.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.910
Analysts say to meet
this increasing demand

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.980
Foxconn's factory in India may eventually

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.253
meet the type of on-campus
accommodation seen in Zhengzhou.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.790
Apple and Foxconn did not
respond to requests for comment

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:41.910
about the challenges facing
facilities in India and Vietnam

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:45.300
such as import delays
and workforce shortages.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:48.210
In Apple's April earnings
call, CEO Tim Cook

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:50.250
said the company's continuing to optimize

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.050
the production process.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.030
- [Tim] Our supply chain is truly global

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:56.970
and so the products are made everywhere.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.980
- [Narrator] Even though Apple
is starting to look elsewhere

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.410
analysts say it's unlikely
to completely leave

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.350
China's efficient system anytime soon.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.730
Production started to recover

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:08.400
after Foxconn lifted COVID-19 restrictions

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.250
at its Zhengzhou plant in early December.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.253
And wait times for high-end
iPhone models have improved.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.690
Still, people involved
in Apple supply chain

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.790
say the company may
look to other suppliers

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:24.660
within China to reduce
its reliance on Foxconn.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.180
That may mean in the future a wider range

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.490
of companies will be
building more of our iPhones

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.306
and other Apple products.

00:03:31.306 --> 00:03:33.889
(upbeat music)

